# "localhost", not 127.0.0.1 - must match the backend's CORS_ORIGINS/
# FRONTEND_URL host (see backend/.env.example) exactly, not just in
# spirit. This isn't cosmetic: the auth cookie is SameSite=Lax, and
# SameSite is scoped to the "site" (host, not just origin) - a frontend
# on localhost:3000 calling an API on 127.0.0.1:8000 is CROSS-SITE, so
# the browser would set the cookie on login but then silently refuse to
# send it back on every following request (an immediate "logs in, then
# every request 401s" symptom). Same host on both sides, different port
# only, keeps every request same-site so the cookie attaches normally.
# See frontend/src/utils/api.js's own comment on this same default for
# the full explanation, including the Windows-IPv6 angle this used to
# be worked around with.
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
REACT_APP_APP_NAME=Woodful Creations
REACT_APP_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Speeds up react-scripts' dev-server compile time meaningfully (a
# well-documented Create React App / webpack lever) - source maps are
# genuinely not needed for normal day-to-day development, only when
# actively debugging a minified stack trace. Uncomment if startup
# still feels slow after the API_URL fix above:
# GENERATE_SOURCEMAP=false
